Sets the maximum number of bytes that can be read.

# Note

If the inner `Buf` has fewer bytes than `lim` then that is the actual
number of available bytes.

# Examples

```rust
use bytes::{Buf, BufMut};

let mut buf = b"hello world".take(2);
let mut dst = vec![];

dst.put(&mut buf);
assert_eq!(*dst, b"he"[..]);

dst.clear();

buf.set_limit(3);
dst.put(&mut buf);
assert_eq!(*dst, b"llo"[..]);
```

